<title>BRAZIL: Ernst &amp; Young to advise on insurance firm sale.</title>
<headline>Ernst &amp; Young to advise on insurance firm sale.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of the Brazilian state of Rio Grande do Sul has hired Ernst &amp; Young and Banco Fator as advisors in the sale of state insurance company Companhia Uniao de Seguros Gerais, a company official said.</p>
<p>Companhia Uniao's president Ney Michelucci said the state government will sell 51 percent of the firm's voting shares by the first half of next year. It will hold on to a minority stake.</p>
<p>Under the contract Ernst &amp; Young will be responsible for evaluating Companhia Uniao's assets and set the minimum price for the sale, he said.</p>
<p>Companhia Uniao is the insurance arm of Banrisul, the Rio Grande do Sul state bank.</p>
<p>In the first half of the year, Companhia Uniao posted premiums of 80.3 million reais, of which 47 percent accounted for life insurance, Michelucci said.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 232 4411.</p>
